{"step_index":1228,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T14:11:14Z","input_tokens":3354,"cache_read_tokens":187382,"output_tokens":1922,"thinking":"The goal is to animate the entry of a computed value into a variable box within the visual calculation stage. The computed value (`anim-source-val`) and target box are identified. A gliding/entering effect will be implemented by animating the `anim-source` visually into the target.\n\n\nThe computed value needs to animate from its source to the target variable box.  The animation will include a smooth slide along an arrow to the variable box. Upon reaching the box, a pulse effect will signal the update. If the variable is updated, the previous value must be visibly struck-through, or slid away, with the new value highlighted with a distinct animation.\n\n\nArithmetic steps will be visually animated with glowing operands that merge, followed by a result burst and an animated arrow indicating storage into a variable. Formula calculations will follow the same visual pipeline.  The currently executing code line will be highlighted with a glowing border and dynamic pointer. Executed or skipped conditional branches will be marked with animated badges.\n\n\nCondition branch animations will emphasize the comparison process. Visual elements will clearly differentiate between executed and skipped branches using distinct visual cues such as glowing borders, dimming, and dashed outlines. Loop transitions will feature smooth slide-in banners and rotating loop icons, with a pass number indicator. Loop visualization will use a pulse on the active cell and a bouncing pointer arrow, with smooth scrolling for array elements.\n\n\nVariables are visually updated with flashing highlights and glowing pills in the scope inspector. Negative resets will display the discarded value with a strike-out and drop effect, followed by a sparkling zero. Animation speed controls scale animation durations via a speed factor, allowing for slower or faster visualizations. Reduced motion settings disable animations entirely, making the experience instant and accessible.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css","EndLine":1345,"StartLine":1285,"toolAction":"Viewing existing keyframes in styles.css","toolSummary":"View existing keyframes in styles.css"}}]}
